attribution_boundary:
  Mike Dupont / meta-introspector owns the upstream Goldbach30 and Goldbach29
  constructions, their 30-to-29 fraction reduction, abstract machines,
  FRACTRAN programs, and Lean proofs fstep_enc at the pinned commit.
  DASHI owns only this immutable provenance receipt plus its independent
  observer/fibre translation, exact arithmetic reconstruction of the success
  macro, and DASHI-native consumer/cost theorems built from that explicitly
  attributed external fact surface.

external_facts_used:
  - Goldbach30 has 30 fractions and 11 control states
  - Goldbach29 has 29 fractions and 10 control states
  - the first 25 annotated rules are shared before the success/failure tail
  - the SA control state is removed in Goldbach29
  - Goldbach30 success uses NT.B -> SA, the SA/SB transfer loop, then SA -> RA.A
  - Goldbach29 success reroutes the transfer through NT.B/SB, stages through
    NT2.B, and reuses the existing NT.B b c -> RA.A transition
  - each upstream file proves one encoded FRACTRAN step matches one abstract
    astep step (fstep_enc)

non_claims:
  - this receipt does not vendor-copy AGPL source into DASHI
  - this receipt does not claim DASHI authorship of Goldbach30 or Goldbach29
  - independent DASHI reconstruction is not the upstream Lean theorem itself
  - this receipt alone does not prove whole-machine reachable weak bisimulation
  - this receipt does not prove Goldbach's conjecture
